<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <AssemblyName>BrickStoreSharp</AssemblyName>
    <Version>1.2.0</Version>
    <AssemblyVersion>1.2.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>1.2.0</FileVersion>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <!-- not every public member is documented yet -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Label="NuGet">
    <PackageId>BrickStoreSharp</PackageId>
    <Authors>Stephan Stapel</Authors>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) Stephan Stapel</Copyright>
    <Description>BrickStoreSharp is a .NET library for reading and writing BrickStore inventory files (*.bsx, https://github.com/rgriebl/brickstore), e.g. to manage LEGO brick inventories for BrickLink and Brick Owl.

Features
* Read and write BrickStore inventory files following BrickStore's BrickStoreXML schema
* Lossless load/save: elements the library does not interpret (e.g. GuiState, DifferenceBaseValues) are written back unchanged
* Typed access to items: type, color, condition, status, quantity, prices, tiered prices, cost, weight, stockroom, markers and more
* Culture-independent number handling and safe saving that never destroys an existing file
* Compatible with .NET Standard 2.0, .NET 8 and .NET 10</Description>
    <PackageTags>brickstore;bricklink;brickowl;lego;inventory;bsx;xml</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/stephanstapel/BrickStoreSharp</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/stephanstapel/BrickStoreSharp</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>1.2.0
New
* Targets .NET Standard 2.0, .NET 8 and .NET 10
* New item properties Reserved, Cost, TotalWeight, MarkerText and MarkerColor
* Elements not interpreted by the library (e.g. DifferenceBaseValues, GuiState) are kept in AdditionalElements and written back unchanged
* Item types unknown to the library are written back unchanged
* Inventory comment is read back when loading
* Faster loading: each item is read in a single pass

Fixed
* Endless recursion when loading from a stream
* File handles not being released after loading
* Prices of 1000 and more were written in a corrupted format; numbers are now written culture-invariant and without rounding
* Status, condition, item type and sub condition are written as BrickStore codes (I/X/E, N/U, ...)
* Currency and BrickLinkChangelogId are read and written as attributes of &lt;Inventory&gt;
* Category, comments, retain, bulk, sale, stockroom, sub condition and tiered prices are no longer lost on save/load
* Default values and empty elements are no longer written
* Saving to a file writes a temporary file first, an existing file is never destroyed by a failed save
* Invalid XML characters throw on save instead of producing unreadable files
* External entities are never resolved when loading (XXE)

Breaking changes
* Synchronous Load/Save throw the original exception instead of an AggregateException
* Missing text elements load as null instead of an empty string
* Items without color are written with ColorID 0 (BrickLink's 'Not Applicable'), as ColorID is required by BrickStore

1.1.0
* More complete mapping of item fields, type safety enhancements and bug fixes

1.0.0
* Initial version</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild>true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
